### Signing material ###
#
# The release keystore is committed. It is not reproducible: regenerating it
# produces a different signature, and an application signed with a new key
# cannot be installed over one signed with the old. Losing it has already cost
# this project one signature change, and every member of the team needs it to
# produce an identical build. For anything published to a store it would belong
# in a secret manager instead, since whoever holds it can sign as the author.
*.jks

### Machine-local ###
#
# Points at an SDK path that differs on every machine, so it is never shared.
local.properties

# Firebase configuration is committed deliberately, so that a checkout runs
# without a setup step. The project is coursework on the free plan; access is
# governed by database.rules.json, which confines a household to its members.
# For anything beyond coursework the service-account key in particular would
# belong in a secret manager, since it bypasses those rules entirely.

### Android / Gradle ###
*.iml
.gradle/
.idea/
.DS_Store
build/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
release/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# Exception: the submitted builds in apk/ are a deliverable and are committed
# deliberately. Build output elsewhere remains excluded by the rule above.
!apk/*.apk

